Pointers:
- kb/reference/adr/019-collection-owned-link-vocabulary.md — 019-Collection-owned link vocabulary with per-destination outbound rules — Each COLLECTION.md owns its outbound-linking rules per destination collection, selecting from a shared authoring catalogue; the connect and write skills read COLLECTION.md directly, and the compiled register-by-register topology is retired
- kb/notes/document-system-README.md — Document system — Index of notes about document types, writing conventions, validation, and structural quality — how notes are classified, structured, and checked
- kb/reference/adr/002-inline-global-types-in-writing-guide.md — 002-inline-global-types-in-writing-guide — Decision to inline note and structured-claim templates into WRITING.md so the agent gets type structure and writing conventions in a single hop — eliminates one read for the two most common note types
- kb/reference/collections-and-types.md — Collections and types — How collections and path-referenced types compose: COLLECTION.md owns register and outbound-link conventions; type specs own structural and semantic contracts resolved directly from type paths
- kb/reference/adr/017-collection-md-is-the-register-convention-boundary.md — 017-collection-md-is-the-register-convention-boundary — Accepted decision to use collection-level COLLECTION.md files as the register convention boundary while keeping types structural and allowing mixed-register collections

